> Can you give an example of what you mean by that?

I'd like to see the full example, but based on the code that is provided, you can do something like this:

```ts
const pageModel = computed(() => {
  const screenWidth = visibilityService.screenWidth();
  const isVideoEnabled = visibilityService.isVideoEnabled();
  const userRole = visibilityService.userRole();

  return page().map((section) => ({
    componentName: section,
    isVisible: isSectionVisible(section, screenWidth, isVideoEnabled, userRole),
  }));
});

// you can use `memoize` function from `lodash` or check another implementation
const isSectionVisible = memoize((
  section: string,
  screenWidth: number,
  isVideoEnabled: boolean,
  userRole: string,
) => {
  /* logic won't be re-executed when it's called again with the same input args */
});
```

I also like what Mike proposed - create `isVisible` signal in the child component:

```html
<!-- parent -->
<app-child *ngFor="let page of pages()" [page]="page"  />
```

```ts
// child
@Component(/* ... */)
export class ChildComponent {
  private visibilityService = inject(VisibilityService);

  page = signal<string | null>(null);
  isVisible = computed(() => {
    const page = this.page();
    const screenWidth = this.visibilityService.screenWidth();
    const isVideoEnabled = this.visibilityService.isVideoEnabled();
    const userRole = this.visibilityService.userRole();

    // check if the page is visible
  });

  // with signal inputs, we'll be able to remove this part
  @Input({ required: true, alias: 'page' })
  set pageInput(page: string) {
    this.page.set(page);
  }
}
```

